  "term": "GAD",
  "definition": "GAD stands for glutamate decarboxylase, an enzyme that converts glutamate into gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA) and carbon dioxide using pyridoxal phosphate as a cofactor. In humans, two forms of this enzyme provide most of the body’s normal GABA supply.",
